WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.106
(playful, twinkling music)

00:00:02.106 --> 00:00:03.351
- [Narrator] This is Zana,

00:00:03.351 --> 00:00:04.803
a Matschie's tree kangaroo.

00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:06.970
She's adorable, isn't she?

00:00:07.883 --> 00:00:10.403
But don't let her
adorableness deceive you.

00:00:10.403 --> 00:00:13.424
This rare kangaroo is
extremely threatened.

00:00:13.424 --> 00:00:17.129
(playful, twinkling music)

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:19.787
With curved claws and
stocky, muscular limbs,

00:00:19.787 --> 00:00:21.781
she's at home in the trees.

00:00:21.781 --> 00:00:24.301
However, her padded paws
allow her to fall from up to

00:00:24.301 --> 00:00:26.218
60 feet without injury.

00:00:27.507 --> 00:00:29.061
This marsupial is so rare,

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:31.791
it can only be found in
the mountainous rainforests

00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:34.769
of northeastern Papua New Guinea.

00:00:34.769 --> 00:00:37.830
It's a solitary creature that
spends most of its time alone,

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.311
except for when there's
a baby to care for.

00:00:41.311 --> 00:00:44.289
Tree kangaroo joeys spend
18 months with their mothers

00:00:44.289 --> 00:00:47.247
before setting out on their own.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.886
Oil drilling and logging

00:00:48.886 --> 00:00:50.990
are destroying the Matschie's habitat

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.477
and it's thick, beautiful
fur has made it an attractive

00:00:53.477 --> 00:00:56.220
target for native hunters.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.181
Captive breeding and
local education efforts

00:00:58.181 --> 00:01:00.070
are making headway,

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.207
but it's future is uncertain.

00:01:03.207 --> 00:01:05.970
This is the Matschie's tree kangaroo.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:09.553
(playful, twinkling music)

